A note on the turtle module
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

packages/runtime/src/python/turtle.py is original work, not a copy of CPython's
turtle. It implements the subset of the documented turtle interface that school
worksheets use, drawing onto a canvas rather than into Tk.

Its circle() reproduces the polygon-approximation approach the standard library
documents — the step count grows with the radius — because an implementation
that does not diverges visibly from the picture a textbook shows. That is an
algorithm, not copied code.

Names outside the supported set raise NotImplementedError naming themselves, so
a teacher meets a clear message rather than a traceback. The supported set is
listed in docs/reference/turtle.md.
